{
  "$comment": [
    "THE single source of truth for every KiriChess rule variable.",
    "",
    "The engine reads this file (embedded into KiriChess.Engine at build time) and the web UI is",
    "generated from it (`npm run gen:rules` -> ui/lib/rules.generated.ts). Nothing else may hardcode",
    "a rule number: the rules page, the custom-game builder, the docs and the engine presets are all",
    "downstream of this document. CI fails if any copy drifts.",
    "",
    "Edit here, then run `npm --prefix ui run gen:rules` to refresh the generated TypeScript and",
    "docs/RULES.md.",
    "",
    "POOL IDENTITY vs POOL NAME. Each pool carries two strings and they are not interchangeable:",
    "  `key`   the frozen storage id. It is written into Games.RatingPool, Ratings.Pool,",
    "          RatingHistory.Pool and Challenge.Pool, it forms the Redis matchmaking queue keys and",
    "          the `bot:{key}` rating namespace, and it is the `preset` value the public API accepts.",
    "          Renaming a key orphans every historical rating row, so treat these six as permanent",
    "          identifiers with no display meaning, the way a database id has none.",
    "  `label` the display name, and the ONLY place a pool's name is written. Change it here and it",
    "          changes everywhere: nothing downstream may hardcode the word. PoolLabelDriftTests",
    "          fails the build if a label literal reappears in ui/ outside the generated files.",
    "",
    "Licence: CC BY 4.0. Attribution: \"KiriChess\" by Michiel Gekiere.",
    "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "edition": "Second Edition",

  "defaults": {
